    // To avoid memory leaks and synchronization issues, we can use cudaMallocAsync and cudaFreeAsync, but that's more complex.
    // Since this is called once per forward, we can allocate and free per call with cudaMalloc/cudaFree; cudaFree will not return until all preceding work in the stream is done? Actually cudaFree is synchronous with device, so it will block until all kernels complete, which is okay but may hurt performance due to sync.
    // For performance, we should use a memory pool or allocate once and reuse. But since we are not allowed to modify .cpp or model_new.py to pass buffers, we have to either allocate each call or use static/global allocations.
